 "is_vocab": false,
 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-idp26892032\" class=\"interactive-embedded-reading\" data-label=\"\">\n<div data-type=\"title\">Link to Learning</div>\n<span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idm39579712\" data-alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20241024.164013/resources/7e78a00326d097ac0ff056021e05539588dbccdf\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\">\n</span>\n<p id=\"fs-idp120599664\">Feedback mechanisms can be understood in terms of driving a race car along a track: watch a short video lesson on positive and negative feedback loops.\n\n</p>\n<div data-type=\"media\" id=\"eip-id2699660\" data-alt=\"feedback_loops\">\n<div class=\"os-has-iframe os-has-link\" data-type=\"switch\">\n<a class=\"os-is-link\" href=\"https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/33-3-homeostasis\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" data-media=\"print\">Access multimedia content</a>\n<iframe width=\"660\" height=\"371.4\" src=\"https://www.openstaxcollege.org/l/feedback_loops\" class=\"os-is-iframe\" data-media=\"screen\"><!-- no-selfclose --></iframe>\n</div>\n                 </div>\n</div>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 521021,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>Voltage-gated sodium channels occur in the cell membranes of nerve cells. They open in response to sodium entering the cell. This  allows more sodium to enter the cell.</p>\n<p>A scientist claims this is a positive feedback loop. What reasoning can be used to justify this claim?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1018393,
     "content_html": "The voltage-gated sodium channels open in response to sodium influx. When a change happens in response to a change in conditions, it makes a positive feedback loop."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018394,
     "content_html": "The voltage-gated sodium channels close when there is enough sodium in the cell. This self regulation means this is an example of a positive feedback loop."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018395,
     "content_html": "The voltage-gated sodium channels open due to sodium and this causes more sodium to go through. The response reinforces the feedback, making this a positive feedback loop."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018396,
     "content_html": "The voltage-gated sodium channels are on the cell membrane. All channels through cell membranes are examples of positive feedback loops. This, this is an examples of a positive feedback loop."
    }
   ],
